OVERVIEW
Thanks for volunteering to be your team's Manager. You play a key role in making sure things run smoothly for both the parents and coaches during the season, as well as creating a sense of community amongst the team and its parents. You handle the logistical tasks off the court so that the coaches can focus on teaching basketball to our kids and families can focus on supporting their athletes.

This handbook gives an overview of the things you'll need to do throughout the season. It should answer the question "What does a JYO Team Manager do?" Throughout the season, you'll get more details and updates from board meetings and emails.

This year, our Team Manager Support Lead (TMSL) will be your go-to contact for any advice or support you need. You can reach the TMSL at teammanagersupport@sanmateojyo.org or via Slack (#2026-team-manager-support). You can also reach out to your coach, fellow JYO Team Managers, and the board on Slack for help — JYO is made up of helpful parent volunteers who are glad to lend a hand.

Emergencies channel: There is a "#2026-Emergencies" channel on Slack where you can reach Commissioners, the President, gym coordinators, and others at any time regarding emergencies such as gym issues, referees not showing up to games, etc.

