Consult with the coach at the start of the season about which tournaments/jamborees they want to participate in, and confirm that some or all of the coaching staff can attend. For events you decide to participate in:
- Send the information to parents and see if you get the minimum number of players required
- Secure commitments before the registration deadline — availability is usually limited, so get your entry form in as soon as possible, and email the tournament coordinator right away to let them know you intend to register
- The registration fee is split among the players' families. The Team Manager can front the registration money for the team if comfortable doing so, then collect fees from parents. Once a family commits to attending, they're obligated to pay their share, since it becomes difficult to coordinate otherwise — set expectations upfront. If a family drops and another player would like to attend (and the tournament allows adding a player), they can work out a payment exchange — be sure to update the registration with the new player
- Turn in fees and registration information before the deadline (for example, each player's parent/guardian typically needs to sign a waiver, and you'll need to fill out the team roster with players' birthdates, grade, and height)
- Be aware that some organizations require additional actions (for example, taking team orders for tournament gear, programs, bentos, etc.). You're the primary point of contact for the tournament before and on the day — if you can't attend, designate a parent as the point of contact to pick up any items (gear, bentos, etc.)
- Some tournaments/jamborees can't accommodate every JYO team that applies (for example, if three JYO teams from the same division apply but only one can get in) — set parent expectations accordingly

To help ensure teams within the same division play a similar number of tournaments or jamborees, we follow this policy:
1. All teams notify other JYO teams in their same grade level of their intent to submit an entry into a jamboree/tournament
2. If more than one JYO team in the same grade is entering the same event, they inform the Jamboree/Tournament Coordinator (as part of the submission, or via a separate email) that if only one JYO team is accepted, the other JYO team may use the accepted bid instead — in the interest of an equal number of jamborees/tournaments across teams. Confirm that your entry form was received

After the registration deadline, confirm whether your team was accepted or not.

Note: If you're canceling practice because you're attending a jamboree or tournament, contact the JYO Board at least one week in advance so we can offer your gym time to another team.

